'' '##_' at the end of a macro body line joins the next end of line.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/pp/src/macro-line-join.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered

'' Mid-body: '1 + 2' folds to 3, and the line AFTER the join still stands on its own --
'' 'qq' is 7 and not part of the sum.
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 3
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 7

'' End of body: the invocation's own EOL is what goes, so '3 + 4' folds to 7 as well.

'' The array initialiser arrives as ONE statement, so all three elements are there.
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 11
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 22
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 99
